  "finalText": "**Root cause:** In `commands.ts:runCli()`, after the build result was known, the status bar was only refreshed in the `finally` block — which runs *after* the `await`ed notification calls (`showInformationMessage`/`showErrorMessage`). Those notifications resolve only when the user dismisses them, so the status bar stayed stuck on \"CodeAtlas: indexing…\" until dismissal.\n\n**Fix** (`apps/extension/src/commands.ts:190-215`):\n- Added `refreshAll()` calls immediately after setting `lastBuildError` (both success and failure paths), **before** the notification `await`.\n- The `finally` block's `refreshAll()` is kept as a safety net. The redundant `client.reload()` was removed since `refresh()` (called by `refreshAll()`) already does it.\n\n**What changed:** 3 `refreshAll()` calls added, 1 `client.reload()` removed — all in `runCli()`. No UI logic altered. The status bar now reflects the actual build outcome immediately, not after the user dismisses a notification.",
